Stale after karr #35. .claude/agents/file-sops-format.md (the file-sops-format briefing) says under "Known ground here":

    **decrypt_file still calls YAML::XS::Dump directly**, bypassing the format
    handler, and therefore has to set the boolean mode itself. That duplication is
    filed as karr #35; it is a live trap, because a change made in the handler
    alone does not reach that path.

That is no longer true: decrypt_file and edit go through File::SOPS::Format::{YAML,JSON}->emit, and a change made in the handler now DOES reach that path -- which inverts the trap. The replacement warning is the other direction: emit is shared with serialize, so a change to the plaintext emitter now moves the encrypted document too, and is therefore wire work rather than format work.

Not edited by the agent that fixed #35: an agent definition is configuration, and a subagent does not change its own briefing. Needs the maintainer.
